        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jacob 2:7",
        "book": "Jacob",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And it supposeth me that they have come up hither to hear the pleasing word of God, yea, the word which healeth the wounded soul.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "Micah 2:7; Alma 31:5; 36:26; Hel. 3:29 (29–30). TG Gospel."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jacob 2:8",
        "book": "Jacob",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore, it burdeneth my soul that I should be constrained, because of the strict commandment which I have received from God, to admonish you according to your crimes, to enlarge the wounds of those who are already wounded, instead of consoling and healing their wounds; and those who have not been wounded, instead of feasting upon the pleasing word of God have daggers placed to pierce their souls and wound their delicate minds.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 131,
            "end": 139,
            "text": "TG Warn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Warn.",
            "prettyString": "TG Warn",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Warn",
                "entryId": "tg-warn",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jacob 2:9",
        "book": "Jacob",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "But, notwithstanding the greatness of the task, I must do according to the strict commands of God, and tell you concerning your wickedness and abominations, in the presence of the pure in heart, and the broken heart, and under the glance of the piercing eye of the Almighty God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "TG Commandments of God."
          },
          {
            "start": 245,
            "end": 253,
            "text": "2 Ne. 9:44. TG God, Omniscience of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Commandments of God.",
            "prettyString": "TG Commandments of God",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Commandments of God",
                "entryId": "tg-commandments-of-god",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jacob 2:10",
        "book": "Jacob",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore, I must tell you the truth according to the plainness of the word of God. For behold, as I inquired of the Lord, thus came the word unto me, saying: Jacob, get thou up into the temple on the morrow, and declare the word which I shall give thee unto this people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "2 Ne. 25:4; 33:5; Jacob 4:13."
