        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And now behold, my brethren, this is the word which I declare unto you, that many of you have begun to search for gold, and for silver, and for all manner of precious ores, in the which this land, which is a land of promise unto you and to your seed, doth abound most plentifully.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 167,
            "end": 171,
            "text": "1 Ne. 18:25; 2 Ne. 5:15 (14–16); Hel. 6:9 (9–11); Ether 9:17; 10:23 (12, 23)."
          },
          {
            "start": 208,
            "end": 223,
            "text": "1 Ne. 4:14; 17:13 (13–14). TG Promised Lands."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jacob 2:12",
        "book": "Jacob",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And the hand of providence hath smiled upon you most pleasingly, that you have obtained many riches; and because some of you have obtained more abundantly than that of your brethren ye are lifted up in the pride of your hearts, and wear stiff necks and high heads because of the costliness of your apparel, and persecute your brethren because ye suppose that ye are better than they.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 189,
            "end": 198,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 14:10; Alma 1:32; 31:25; Morm. 8:28 (28, 36–40)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jacob 2:13",
        "book": "Jacob",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, my brethren, do ye suppose that God justifieth you in this thing? Behold, I say unto you, Nay. But he condemneth you, and if ye persist in these things his judgments must speedily come unto you.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jacob 2:14",
        "book": "Jacob",
        "chapter": 2,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "O that he would show you that he can pierce you, and with one glance of his eye he can smite you to the dust!",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG God, Indignation of; God, Omniscience of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG God, Indignation of; God, Omniscience of.",
            "prettyString": "TG God, Indignation of; TG God, Omniscience of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
